hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3524","A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I am undone. He asked him: What has happened to you ? He said: I had intercourse with my wife in Ramadan (while I was fasting). He asked: Can you set a slave free ? He said: No. He again asked: Can you fast for two consecutive months ? He said: No. He asked: Can you provide food for sixty poor people ? He said: No. He said: Sit down. Then a huge basket containing dates ('araq) was brought to the Prophet ﷺ. He then said to him: Give it as sadaqah (i.e. alms). He said: Messenger of Allah, there is no poorer family than mine between the two lave plains of it (Medina). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed so that his eye-teeth became visible, and said: Give it to your family to eat. Musaddad said in another place: ""his canine teeth"". (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2390)"
"3525","I do not have the means for that either. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) gave him dates and instructed him to give them as charity. The narrator says: He mentioned his own neediness before the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), so the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) instructed him to take them for himself."
"3526","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Woe to you, what has happened?"" He replied, ""I had intercourse with my wife during the day in the month of Ramadan."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Free a slave."" He replied, ""I do not have one."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Then fast for two consecutive months."" He replied, ""I am not able to do that."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Then feed sixty needy people."" He replied, ""I do not have the means."" A basket containing fifteen saa’ of dates was presented to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Give this as charity."" He replied, ""Should I give it in charity to people poorer than my family? There is no one in the whole city more in need than my household."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) smiled until his molar teeth became visible. He said, ""Take it, seek forgiveness from Allah, and feed it to your family."
"3527","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, ""What has happened?"" He replied, ""I had intercourse with my wife during the day in the month of Ramadan."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Free a slave."" He replied, ""I do not have one."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Then fast for two consecutive months."" He replied, ""I am not able to do that."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Then feed sixty needy people."" He replied, ""I do not have the means."" The narrator says: A basket of dates was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He said, ""Take this and give it as charity."" He said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Should I give it to anyone other than my own family? By the One in Whose hand is my soul, there is no one in all of Madinah more in need than me."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) smiled until his molar teeth became visible. Then he said, ""Take it and seek forgiveness from your Lord."
"3528","The Prophet (peace be upon him) inquired about his matter, so he mentioned that he had intercourse with his wife during Ramadan (while fasting). A container was brought to the Prophet (peace be upon him), which was called 'araq.' It contained dates. The Prophet (peace be upon him) inquired: Where is the man who has been ruined? That person stood up. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Give this as charity."
"3529","While we were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ a man came and said, ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! I have been ruined."" Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked what was the matter with him. He replied ""I had sexual intercourse with my wife while I was fasting."" Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him, ""Can you afford to manumit a slave?"" He replied in the negative. Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him, ""Can you fast for two successive months?"" He replied in the negative. The Prophet ﷺ asked him, ""Can you afford to feed sixty poor persons?"" He replied in the negative. The Prophet ﷺ kept silent and while we were in that state, a big basket full of dates was brought to the Prophet ﷺ . He asked, ""Where is the questioner?"" He replied, ""I (am here)."" The Prophet ﷺ said (to him), ""Take this (basket of dates) and give it in charity."" The man said, ""Should I give it to a person poorer than I? By Allah; there is no family between its (i.e. Medina's) two mountains who are poorer than I."" The Prophet ﷺ smiled till his premolar teeth became visible and then said, 'Feed your family with it."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1936)"
"3530","“A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, my sister has died and she owed a fast of two consecutive months.’ He said: ‘Do you not think that if your sister owed a debt, you would pay it off for her?’ She said: ‘Of course.’ He said: ‘The right of Allah is greater.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1758)"
"3531","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had himself cupped when he was fasting and wearing ihram (pilgrim garb). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2373)"
"3532","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saw a man who was having cupping done, so the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The fast of the one who does cupping and the one who gets it done is broken."
"3533","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The one who performs cupping and the one who gets cupped, their fast is broken. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): Abu Qilabah also heard this narration from Abu Asma from Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him), and he also heard this narration from Abu Ash'ath from Abu Asma from Sayyiduna Shaddad bin Aws (may Allah be pleased with him), so both chains are preserved. Shayban bin Abdur Rahman combined both chains of this narration transmitted from Yahya bin Abu Kathir, which is narrated from Abu Qilabah from Abu Asma from Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him), and from Abu Ash'ath from Abu Asma from Sayyiduna Shaddad bin Aws (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"3534","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man who was getting cupped, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who does cupping and the one who gets cupped, their fast is broken."
"3535","‘The cupper and the one for whom cupping is done both break their fast.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1679)"
"3536","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) instructed Sayyiduna Abu Taybah to present himself before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) at the time of sunset. Then he directed him to bring the cupping instruments at the time of iftar and perform cupping on the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked him: ""How much is your tax?"" He replied: ""Two sa’."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had one sa’ remitted for him. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): The narrator named Sa’id bin Yahya is known by the name Sa’dan. He belongs to the people of Damascus. He is trustworthy and reliable, and in hadith, he is upright in his affairs."
"3537","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would sometimes kiss one of his noble wives while he was fasting. Then Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) smiled."
"3538","Should one observing fast kiss (his wife)? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: Ask her (Umm Salama). She informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did that, where upon he said: Messenger of Allah, Allah pardoned thee all thy sins, the previous and the later ones. Upon this the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ) said: By Allah, I am the most God conscious among you and I fear Him most among you. (Using translation from Muslim 1108)"
"3539","'A'isha (Allah be pleased with her) reported that Allah's Apostle (peace be upon him) kissed (his wives) while fasting. (Using translation from Muslim 1106m)"
"3540","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to kiss one of his noble wives while he was fasting."
"3541","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss me when he was fasting and when I was fasting. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2384)"
"3542","Hafsa (Allah be pleased with her) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissed (his wives) while fasting. (Using translation from Muslim 1107a)"
"3543","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to kiss when he was fasting, and who among you can control his desire as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to control his desire?” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1684)"
"3544","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked: What is that? I replied: I kissed (my wife) while I was fasting. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you think, if you rinse your mouth with water (what will happen to your fast)? I replied: In that case, there will be no harm. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then how is this (any different)?"
"3545","I asked Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): Was it during an obligatory fast or a voluntary fast? Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) replied: In both, in the obligatory and in the voluntary fast. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): Abu Salamah bin Abdur Rahman heard this narration from Umar bin Abdul Aziz, from Urwah, from Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her). He also heard this narration directly from Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her). And the evidence for its authenticity is this: Ma'mar has stated this; this narration is transmitted from Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, who says: I asked Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) whether it was about the obligatory or the voluntary fast? So, on one occasion, he narrated this from Umar bin Abdul Aziz, from Urwah, from Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), and on another occasion, he narrated it directly from Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"3546","I was fasting, the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would not touch any part of my face."
"3547","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to kiss one of his noble wives while he was fasting, then she smiled. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) had the greatest control over his desires. Even so, he used to kiss his wives while fasting. Through this, the intention is to teach that whoever has control over his desires, it is permissible for him to do such an act while fasting. However, when his wives were fasting, the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would refrain from such acts. Because he knew that for women, in such a situation, it is difficult to control themselves. So the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would abstain from this act and let their condition remain. When they were in that state, in this way, there remains no contradiction or difference between the two narrations."
"3548","‘It is not an act of righteousness to fast while traveling.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1664)"
"3549","These people are the disobedient ones; these are the disobedient ones. (Using translation from Muslim 1114a)"
"3550","I am mounted, I am in an easier state than you, you people are walking on foot. The people again began to look towards the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), so the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) moved to his side. You drank water, so the people also drank water."
"3551","The people were also fasting. Then he asked for a cup of water, raised it, and the people began to look at him, so he drank it. After that, it was submitted to him that some people were still fasting, so the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""They are disobedient people."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called them disobedient because when he commanded them to break their fast during the journey, they did not act upon this command. This does not mean that those people became disobedient merely because of fasting during the journey, because both fasting and not fasting during travel are absolutely permissible."
"3552","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saw a man around whom people had gathered and were providing shade for him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) inquired: What is the matter? The people replied: This man is observing a fast. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: It is not an act of righteousness that you fast while traveling."
"3553","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: It is not an act of righteousness that you fast while traveling."
"3554","the Messenger of Allah saw some people gathered around a man, so he asked (what was happening) and they said: ""It is a man who is exhausted because of fasting."" The Messenger of Allah said: ""It is not righteousness to fast when traveling."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2257)"
"3555","The narrator states: The companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him) used to follow the actions that came after from him."
"3556","I am commanding you. The people again began to look towards him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) moved to his side (and advanced) and drank water, so the people also drank water."
"3557","""Some food was brought to the Messenger of Allah at Marr Az-Zahran, and he said to Abu Bakr and 'Umar: 'Come and eat.' They said: 'We are fasting.' He said: 'Saddle the camels for your companions, and help your companions.""'(Daif) (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2264)"
"3558","""We were on a journey with the Messenger of Allah. Some of us were fasting and some of us broke their fast. The one who broke their fast had no objection to the one who fasted, and the one who fasted had no objection to the one who broke his fast. They saw that whoever had the strength to fast then that was good, and whoever was weak, then breaking it was better."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 713)"
"3559","narrates: We were traveling with the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). Some of us were fasting and some were not. On a very hot day, we stopped at a place. Some of us were shielding ourselves from the sun with our hands, and the person who had a cloak had the most shade, and the fasting people were using it for shade. Those who were not fasting got up, pitched tents, and took care of the mounts, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Today, those who did not fast have taken the reward."
"3560","""If you wish then fast and if you wish then do not fast."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2308)"
"3561","We travelled along with the Prophet ﷺ during Ramadan. Some of us were fasting and other broke their fast. Those who fasted did not find fault with those who broke, and those who broke their fast did not find fault with those who fasted. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2405)"
"3562","narrates: We set out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the seventeenth of (the month of) Ramadan; this was the occasion when Makkah was conquered. Some people were fasting and some people were not fasting, and neither group objected to the other."
"3563","narrates: On the occasion of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) set out during the month of Ramadan. He kept the fast until he reached Kudayd. Then he broke his fast, and those who were with him also broke their fast. So, people used to follow the matter that occurred after the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him)."
"3564","The narrator states: The companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him) used to follow whatever happened after him."
"3565","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) traveled during the month of Ramadan. For one of his companions, fasting became a cause of hardship. His camel took him to the shade of a tree. When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was informed about this, he ordered him to break his fast. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) called for a vessel containing water, took it in his hand, and when the people saw that he had drunk the water, they also drank the water (and broke their fast)."
"3566","Ibn ʿAbbas said, ""Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out from Medina to Mecca and he fasted till he reached 'Usfan, where he asked for water and raised his hand to let the people see him, and then broke the fast, and did not fast after that till he reached Mecca, and that happened in Ramadan."" Ibn ʿAbbas used to say, ""Messenger of Allah ﷺ (sometimes) fasted and (sometimes) did not fast during the journeys so whoever wished to fast could fast, and whoever wished not to fast, could do so."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1948)"
"3567","""I feel able to fast while traveling; is there any sin on me?"" He said: ""It is a concession from Allah, the mighty and sublime, so whoever accepts it has done well, and whoever wants to fast, there is no sin on him."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2303)"
"3568","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Indeed, Allah Almighty likes that His concession be acted upon just as He likes that His obligatory command be acted upon."
"3569","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Whoever died and he ought to have fasted (the missed days of Ramadan) then his guardians must fast on his behalf."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1952)"
"3570","“A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, my sister has died and she owed a fast of two consecutive months.’ He said: ‘Do you not think that if your sister owed a debt, you would pay it off for her?’ She said: ‘Of course.’ He said: ‘The right of Allah is greater.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1758)"
"3571","I have come to know that you observe voluntary fasts every day and spend the whole night in voluntary prayers. I replied: Yes, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Do not do so; (at night) you should also sleep and also offer voluntary prayers, (during the day) you should also observe voluntary fasts and also leave them, because your body has a right over you, your guest has a right over you, your wife has a right over you. I am giving you the option that you may fast three days in every month; every good deed is rewarded tenfold, so this will be equivalent to fasting the whole month. I submitted: O Messenger of Allah! (I feel capable of fasting more than this.) The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then fast three days in every week. The narrator says: I insisted on more, so more was prescribed for me. I submitted: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! I feel capable of more than this. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then fast as the Prophet of Allah, Sayyiduna Dawud (peace be upon him), used to fast, and do not fast more than that. I asked: What was the method of fasting of the Prophet of Allah, Sayyiduna Dawud (peace be upon him)? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Half of the time (i.e., fasting one day and not fasting the next day). (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): The statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), ""Your visitor also has a right over you,"" these words are narrated only in this narration, and in this is evidence that when a guest or visitor comes to the house, it is permissible for a person to break (voluntary) fasts."
"3572","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a woman's husband is present at home, she should not fast without his permission."
"3573","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman whose husband is present should not fast on any day other than Ramadan without his permission."
"3574","I am not like you. My Lord gives me food and drink."
"3575","The Prophet ﷺ said (to his companions), ""Do not fast Al-Wisal."" They said, ""But you fast Al-Wisail."" He said, ""I am not like you, for at night my Lord feeds me and makes me drink."" But the people did not give up Al-Wisal, so the Prophet ﷺ fasted Al-Wisal with them for two days or two nights, and then they saw the crescent whereupon the Prophet ﷺ said, ""If the crescent had delayed, I would have continued fasting (because of you),"" as if he wanted to vanquish them completely (because they had refused to give up Al Wisal). (Using translation from Bukhārī 7299)"
"3576","I am not like you in this matter. I spend the night in such a state that my Lord gives me food and drink. You should only take upon yourselves as much as you have the strength to do."
"3577","I spend the night in such a state that the One who feeds gives me food and the One who gives drink gives me drink. If any of you wishes to observe continuous fasting, then let him do so from one morning till the next morning."" (That is, from one pre-dawn meal (suhoor) to the next, meaning at the time of breaking the fast, he should not eat or drink anything as usual.)"
"3578","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Fasting cannot be joined together (i.e., Saum Wisal cannot be observed)."
"3579","I am not like you. I am given food and drink."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): This narration is evidence that all those narrations in which it is mentioned that the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, tied stones to his stomach are all false. The meaning is that the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, tied a waist-wrapper (tehband) there. It does not mean tying stones, and the word ""hijz"" refers to the end of the waist-wrapper. The reason is: Allah Almighty used to feed and give drink to His Messenger. When he used to observe continuous fasting, how could Allah Almighty leave him hungry at that time, when he had not even observed continuous fasting and needed to tie stones to his stomach, whereas stones cannot remove hunger."
"3580","Sayyidah Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) never fasted an entire month except for Ramadan, nor did he ever leave fasting for an entire month. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not fast in any other month as much as he fasted in Sha'ban."
"3581","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): \""Whoever always (i.e., daily) observes voluntary fasting, then in reality, he has neither fasted nor left fasting.\"""""""
"3582","""It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, so and so never broke his fast, even for one day for the rest of his life.' He said: 'He has neither fasted nor broken his fast."""" 'Ata said: ""someone who heard him told me that Ibn 'Umar (said) that the Prophet said: 'Whoever fasts every day of his life, then he has not fasted."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2379)"
"3583","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) indicated this by making the number ninety. By this, he"""""
"3584","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \""Whoever always (i.e., daily observes voluntary fasting), Hell will be made so narrow for him.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) indicated this by making the figure of ninety. The narrator named Fadl narrated these words the second time: \""The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) closed his fist at ninety.\"" (Imam Ibn Hibban, m"
"3585","I am fasting. So Sayyiduna Ammar bin Yasir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whoever fasts on the day about which there is doubt (whether it is a day of Ramadan or not), then that person has disobeyed Sayyiduna Abul Qasim (the Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him)."
"3586","‘Do not anticipate Ramadan by fasting one or two days before, except for a man who has a habitual pattern of fasting, in which case let him fast.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1650)"
"3587","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him, or perhaps to another person: Have you fasted any days from the end of this month? He replied: No. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When you do not fast (any voluntary fasts) in a month, then fast one or two days."
"3588","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked a man: Did you fast the last day of Sha'ban ? He replied: No. He said: If you did not observe a fast, you must fast for a day. One of the two narrators said: For two days. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2328)"
"3589","the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""When it is the middle of ˹the month of˺ Shaʿbān then break ˹from˺ fasting until ˹the month of˺ Ramaḍān arrives.”[^1]"
"3590","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not welcome (the month of) Ramadan by fasting before it (i.e., do not start fasting before its beginning). Start fasting by sighting it (i.e., the crescent of the first of Ramadan), and celebrate Eid al-Fitr by sighting it. If there is a cloud barrier between you and it (the crescent), or there is difficulty in sighting, then complete the count to thirty."
"3591","from the Prophet ﷺ who said, ""There ˹should be˺ no fasting after the middle of ˹the month of˺ Shaʿbān until the month of Ramaḍān arrives.”"
"3592","‘Do not anticipate Ramadan by fasting one or two days before, except for a man who has a habitual pattern of fasting, in which case let him fast.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1650)"
"3593","The month of Ramadan may consist of twenty-nine days. So do not fast till you have sighted it (the new moon) and do not break fast, till you have sighted it (the new moon of Shawwal), and if the sky is cloudy for you, then calculate. (Using translation from Muslim 1080e)"
"3594","""The Messenger of Allah said: ""The Messenger of Allah said: Do not fast before Ramadan. Fast when you see it and stop fasting when you see it, and if clouds prevent you from seeing it, then complete Thirty (Days).""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2130)"
"3595","I am fasting. Sayyiduna Ammar bin Yasir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whoever fasts on a day about which he is doubtful, then he has disobeyed Sayyiduna Abul Qasim (the Prophet Muhammad) (peace be upon him)."
"3596","Sayyiduna Ammar bin Yasir (may Allah be pleased with him) on a day about which there was doubt as to whether it was Ramadan or not. A goat was brought, so a person withdrew. Sayyiduna Ammar bin Yasir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whoever fasts on this day has disobeyed Sayyiduna Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"3597","""Do not fast until you see the crescent, and do not stop fasting until you see it, and if it is obscured from you (too cloudy), then work it out."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2121)"
"3598","Abu Huraira (Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting on these two days. 'Id-ul-Adha and 'Id-ul-Fitr. (Using translation from Muslim 1138)"
"3599","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Fasting is a shield.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2224)"
"3600","The narrator named Abu Ubaid says: I also participated in the Eid prayer behind Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him). He arrived and performed the prayer. When he completed the prayer, he addressed the people in a sermon and said: Today, two Eids have come together for you (i.e., today is Eid and also Friday), so whoever among the people of the surrounding areas wishes to wait for Jumu'ah, let him wait, and whoever wishes to return, let him return. I give him permission. The narrator named Abu Ubaid says: Then I participated in the Eid prayer behind Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) at a time when Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) had been confined to his house. He arrived and performed the prayer. When he completed the prayer, he addressed the people in a sermon."",""Abu Ubaid said"",""""""Then I witnessed the Eid with Uthman ibn Affan. He came"","" prayed"","" then turned and addressed the people"","" saying"","" 'Today"","" two Eids have coincided for you. Whoever from the residents of the higher areas wishes to wait for the Friday prayer"","" let him wait"","" and whoever wishes to return"","" let him return"","" for I have granted him permission.'"",""Abu Ubaid said"",""""""Then I witnessed the Eid with Ali ibn Abi Talib while Uthman was present. He came"","" prayed"","" then turned and addressed the people."""""""""
"3601","“The days of Mina (11th, 12th, and 13th of Dhul-Hijjah) are days of eating and drinking.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1719)"
"3602","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The days of Tashreeq are days of eating, drinking, and remembering Allah."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): The statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) that ""they are days of eating"" is a literal notification. By this is meant the prohibition of fasting during the days of Tashreeq, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade fasting on these days by using the words that eating is permissible, and said that ""they are days of eating."" And as for the statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) that ""they are days of remembering Allah,"" by this he intended recommendation and guidance."
"3603","""The day of Arafat and the day of sacrifice and the day of At-Tashriq are our Id, the people of Islam, and they are days of eating and drinking."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3004)"
"3604","""Ibn Umar was asked about fasting (the Day of) Arafah (at Arafat). He said: 'I performed Hajj with the Prophet, and he did not fast it, and with Abu Bakr, and he did not fast it, and with Umar, and he did not fast it, and with Uthman, and he did not fast it. I do no fast it, nor order it nor forbid it."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 751)"
"3605","The narrator states: Sayyidah Umm Fadl (may Allah be pleased with her) told me that on the day of Arafah, milk was presented to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he drank it."
"3606","""While the people were with me on the day of ʿArafat they differed as to whether the Prophet ﷺ was fasting or not; some said that he was fasting while others said that he was not fasting. So, I sent to him a bowl full of milk while he was riding over his camel and he drank it."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1988)"
"3607","narrates: People were in doubt regarding the matter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Arafah, so Sayyida Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) sent a bowl (of milk) to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). At that time, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was standing at the place of stay. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank it while the people were watching him. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): On the occasion of the Farewell Hajj, the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were with him. Similarly, a group of his relatives was also with him, so it is possible that Sayyida Umm Fadl (may Allah be pleased with her) and Sayyida Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) were present at the same place in Arafat, and that bowl of milk was taken to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from both of these women. Thus, in one narration, the bowl and its sending have been attributed to Sayyida Umm Fadl (may Allah be pleased with her), and in another narration, to Sayyida Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"3608","I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fasting during the first ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2439)"
"3609","I did not forbid fasting on Friday, rather, by the Lord of the Ka'bah! Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it."
"3610","Abdul Malik bin Umair, narrating from a man belonging to Banu Harith bin Ka'b, whose name was Abu Awbar, reports: I was sitting with Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) when a man came to him and said: You have forbidden people from fasting on Friday. He replied: I have not forbidden people from fasting on Friday, rather I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: ""Do not fast on Friday, because it is a day of Eid, except if you join another day with it (then the ruling is different)."" Imam Ibn Hibban (may Allah have mercy on him) says: The statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ""in days"" refers to any one day."
"3611","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) came to the house of Lady Juwayriya bint al-Harith (may Allah be pleased with her) on a Friday. She w"
"3612","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not single out the night of Friday among the other nights for performing voluntary prayers, and do not single out the day of Friday among the other days for fasting."
"3613","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not single out Friday among the rest of the days for fasting, and do not single out the night of Friday among the rest of the nights for performing voluntary prayers."
"3614","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: None of you must fast on Friday unless he fasts the day before or the day after. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2420)"
"3615","I pledged allegiance on the blessed hand of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). I heard him say: 'Do not fast on Saturday, except for the fast that is obligatory upon you. And if a person finds only the root of a tree to chew (to break the fast on Saturday), then he should break his fast with that.'"
"3616","The Prophet (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) used to say: These two days are the festivals of the polytheists (they eat and drink on these days), so I wish to act contrary to them."
"3617","The people replied: Some of us have eaten something and some have not eaten anything. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever among you has not eaten anything should observe the fast, and whoever has eaten something, then he should complete the rest of the day (as a fast), and inform the people of the surrounding areas that they should also complete the rest of the day (i.e., not eat anything)."
"3618","I asked: If I find them in a state that they have already eaten something, then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: They should complete the fast till the end of the day (i.e., they should not eat anything further)."
"3619","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) sent a man from the tribe of Aslam to announce among the people: “Today is the day of Ashura. Whoever has eaten something should not eat anything for the rest of the day, and whoever has not eaten or drunk anything should observe the fast.”"
"3620","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a message in the morning of the day of ‘Ashura to the settlements of the Ansar around Madinah, saying that whoever is fasting should complete his fast, and whoever has eaten should observe fasting for the rest of the day (i.e., should not eat or drink any more). Sayyida Rubayyi’ (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: We used to fast on that day, and we used to make our small children fast as well. We would take them with us to the mosque and make dolls out of flour for them. When any one of them cried for food, we would give that to him, until it was time to break the fast (then we would break our fast)."
"3621","The Quraish used to fast on the day of 'Ashurah in pre Islamic days. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would fast on it in pre-Islamic period. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Medina, he fasted on it and commanded to fast on it. When the fast of Ramadan was prescribed, that became obligatory, and (fasting on) 'Ashurah was abandoned. He who wishes may fast on it and he who wishes may leave it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2442)"
"3622","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said regarding fasting on the day of Ashura, this was after the command of fasting in R"
"3623","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates: The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""The day of Ashura is such a day that in the days of ignorance people used to fast on it, so whoever among you wishes to fast on this day may do so, and whoever dislikes it may leave it.\"""""""
"3624","We, during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, in one month of Ramadan (observed fast according to our liking). He who wished to fast lasted and he who wished to break broke it and fed a needy person as an expiation 1544 till this verse was revealed:"" He who witnesses among you the month (of Ramadan) he should observe fast during it"" (ii. 184). (Using translation from Muslim 1145b)"
"3625","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked them: What is the reason for this? They replied: This is a great day in which Allah Almighty granted deliverance to Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) and drowned Pharaoh and his followers, so Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) fasted on this day to thank Allah Almighty. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: We are closer to Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) than you and more deserving of fasting on this day. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) fasted on this day and also ordered fasting on this day."
"3626","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say this: ""This is the day of Ashura. Fasting on this day has not been made obligatory upon you, but I am fasting. So whoever wishes to fast on this day may do so."
"3627","The Jews used to consider the day of Ashura as a festival. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You should act contrary to them; you should fast on (the day of) Ashura."
"3628","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then I will fast."" Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Then, on the same day, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to me a second time. I said: ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! We have been given 'Hais' as a gift, and we have saved it for you."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Present it."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had been fasting, but then he broke his fast."
"3629","I replied: No. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Then I will fast."
"3630","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said, ""This morning, I had intended to fast."" Then he asked for the food and ate it."
"3631","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: It is equal to fasting for a whole year. He asked: What is your opinion about a person who fasts on the day of Arafah? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: It wipes out the sins of the previous year and the coming year."
"3632","I hope from Allah Almighty that it expiates the sins of the previous year and the coming year (and that one year), and regarding fasting on the day of Ashura, I hope from the grace of Allah Almighty that it expiates the sins of the previous year."
"3633","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) while he was sitting by the well of Zamzam, leaning against his cloak. I sat down beside him; he was a very excellent companion. I asked him about Ashura: so he sat up straight. Then he asked: Do you want to ask about it in any particular regard? I asked: About its fasting—on which day should we fast? He said: When you see the crescent of Muharram, start counting, then fast on the ninth day. I asked: Did Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) also fast like this? He replied: Yes."
"3634","“Whoever fasts Ramadan then follows it with six days of Shawwal, it is as if he fasted for a lifetime.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1716)"
"3635","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whoever fasts the fasts of Ramadan and then fasts six days of Shawwal, it is as if he has fasted for the whole year."
"3636","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The best fasting after the month of Ramadan is the month of Allah, Al-Muharram, and the best prayer is prayer at night.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1613)"
"3637","The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to observe so many voluntary fasts in a month that we would think he would continue fasting, and then he would abandon voluntary fasting (in a month) to the extent that we would think he would not fast. I did not see the Prophet (peace be upon him) fasting in any month more than in Sha'ban, apart from Ramadan. The Prophet (peace be upon him) would not fast on some days of Sha'ban, but would fast for the rest of the month."
